The crypto + wire-format CORE (src/airplay_crypto.*) was reconstructed
clean-room from public reverse-engineering work (owntone, pyatv, shairport-sync,
pair_ap, emanuelecozzi's AP2 notes, the unofficial AirPlay spec) read as
documentation only; no upstream code is copied into it.

The RAOP / AirPlay sender logic in src/raop_sender.cpp is in part a C++ PORT of
pyatv (MIT, (c) 2020 Pierre Ståhl), its RTSP/RTP/sync/timing model and the
HAP pairing sequence follow pyatv's raop/auth modules. No Python code is
bundled; pyatv's MIT notice is reproduced in licenses/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.

Ported / spec-referenced protocol logic and vendored / build-time dependencies
keep their own licenses (full texts in licenses/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt):
